    <p><strong>Why is my water pressure bad everywhere?</strong></p>
    <p>On a pre-1965 home, almost always galvanized supply pipe rusted closed from the inside. Hot worse than cold confirms it. Spot fixes just move the next failure downstream.</p>

    <p><strong>How long should my water heater last?</strong></p>
    <p>8 to 12 years here. Rust at the base means replace now — that is the tank itself failing, and it has no repair.</p>

    <p><strong>All my drains are slow at once — what is it?</strong></p>
    <p>A main-line problem, not a fixture. Get a camera down the cleanout before anyone snakes it, especially on the older cast-iron streets.</p>

